1
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:21,177
Hello, I'm Matt Silver, and this is an article from our new series 'Eating around the world'.

2
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:26,773
I'm writing this from Kulusuk, an Inuit village in Greenland.

3
00:00:26,773 --> 00:00:36,720
It's a pleasant place in summer, with mild temperatures and fantastic views of the icebergs on the sea just in front of the village.

4
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:40,940
It's a popular place for tourists in those months.

5
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:49,911
But winters are long and hard, and the life for the 250 people in the village isn't easy at all.

6
00:00:49,911 --> 00:00:55,340
The roads are covered in ice, and the sea is frozen, too.

7
00:00:56,480 --> 00:01:00,314
The Inuits don't have a lot of choices for food.

8
00:01:00,980 --> 00:01:05,620
The summer is too short and not long enough for the Inuits to grow vegetables.

9
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:09,860
They sometimes find berries during the warmer months.

10
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:11,960
And they eat seaweed.

11
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:17,680
But there are no other vegetables, so they don't eat enough greens.

12
00:01:17,680 --> 00:01:25,340
There is a shop in the village, but during the winter it doesn't get any fresh vegetables.

13
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:31,510
This is why the Inuits eat lots of raw and boiled meat.

14
00:01:32,240 --> 00:01:41,180
They eat sea animals – seals, whales and fish – and they eat reindeer and other land animals.

15
00:01:41,180 --> 00:01:48,060
These animals have a lot of fat on them because it keeps them warm in the freezing temperatures.

16
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:52,200
Do the Inuits eat too much fat?

17
00:01:53,020 --> 00:01:54,700
Isn't that very dangerous?

18
00:01:55,840 --> 00:02:04,262
Well, here's the surprise: in the western world, people say 'Don't eat too much fat!'

19
00:02:04,262 --> 00:02:15,233
But the Inuits eat a lot of animal fat and they are healthy, perhaps because they eat boiled rather than fried meat.

20
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:22,320
Life for the people from Kulusuk can be difficult but they are healthy.

21
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:26,060
Maybe we can learn a lot from them!
